# Line endings for the files whose bytes are a claim.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is enabled on at least one maintainer machine, so a text file
# without an attribute here is checked out CRLF on Windows and LF everywhere
# else. That is normally harmless. It is not harmless for a license notice: the
# whole point of `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` is that each file below is
# byte-for-byte what the upstream project publishes, recorded by sha256. A
# platform-dependent checkout would make every one of those hashes wrong on one
# of the two platforms, and `test/license_distribution_test.dart` compares them.
#
# So: pin every notice to LF, on every platform, and mark the redistributed
# binaries binary so nothing ever tries to translate them.
#
# NOTE: this file deliberately does NOT normalise the whole repository. 51 of
# the 112 files the registry hashes currently carry CRLF in a Windows worktree,
# which makes the generated registry's sha256 values platform-dependent. That is
# a real cross-platform defect, but fixing it re-normalises several hundred
# files and regenerates every registry hash, so it belongs in its own reviewed
# change alongside the CI matrix that would catch it — not smuggled into the
# licensing commit.

# Elattar's own license, and the notices installed into consumer projects.
LICENSE                     text eol=lf
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md      text eol=lf

# Verbatim upstream license texts. Byte fidelity here is the deliverable.
third_party/**              text eol=lf

# Redistributed binaries. Never translate these.
*.ttf                       binary
*.otf                       binary
*.woff                      binary
*.woff2                     binary
*.png                       binary
*.jpg                       binary
*.jpeg                      binary
*.ico                       binary
